Dear Quality Assurance & Pharmacovigilance Team,

I am writing to urgently report a severe adverse reaction observed in our inpatient pediatric ward this morning involving your product Amoxicillin 250mg Oral Suspension.

Product & Dispensing Details:
- Product: Amoxicillin 250mg / 5mL Oral Suspension
- Batch / Lot Number: AX-2209-B
- Expiry Date: 11/2027
- Patient: 7-year-old male inpatient (Ward 4B)
- Administration Time: 08:15 AM

Clinical Presentation:
Within 20 minutes of receiving the first 5mL dose reconstituted from the supplied bottle, the patient developed acute bilateral facial erythema, an extensive urticarial maculopapular rash across the torso, profuse diaphoresis, and sudden-onset severe dizziness accompanied by hypotension (blood pressure dropped to 80/45 mmHg).

Medical Intervention:
Immediate emergency stabilization was administered (intramuscular epinephrine 0.15mg, IV hydrocortisone, and supplemental oxygen). The patient has stabilized and remains under close hemodynamic monitoring in our intensive care unit.

Visual Inspection of Suspension:
Upon inspecting the remaining reconstituted suspension, nursing staff observed unusual dark particulate matter suspended throughout the liquid that failed to disperse despite standard shaking.

The container and remaining liquid have been quarantined in our pharmacy cold store under chain-of-custody lock. Please initiate immediate pharmacovigilance logging and arrange for sample retrieval and batch recall assessment.

